description:
Wire the sieve feature flag in both Cargo.toml files and lib.rs files.

WHAT: Feature flag plumbing so sieve types and handlers are compiled when --features sieve is passed.

ALGORITHM:
1. crate-jmap-mail-types/Cargo.toml: add sieve = [] to [features] (done as part of JMAP-wx3, verify it is present)
2. crate-jmap-mail-server/Cargo.toml: add sieve = ["jmap-mail-types/sieve"] to [features]
3. crate-jmap-mail-server/src/lib.rs: add (each item gated individually):
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")] pub mod sieve;
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")] pub use jmap_mail_types::sieve::JMAP_SIEVE_SCRIPTS_URI;
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")] pub use sieve::SieveBackend;
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")] pub use sieve::{handle_sieve_get, handle_sieve_set, handle_sieve_query, handle_sieve_validate};
4. crate-jmap-mail-server/src/lib.rs: add register_sieve_handlers function (gated):
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")]
   pub fn register_sieve_handlers<B, C>(dispatcher: &mut Dispatcher<C>, backend: Arc<B>)
   where B: MailBackend + sieve::SieveBackend + 'static, C: Clone + Send + 'static {
     reg!("SieveScript/get", backend, |b, _ci, a| sieve::handle_sieve_get(&*b, a).await);
     reg!("SieveScript/set", backend, |b, _ci, a| sieve::handle_sieve_set(&*b, a).await);
     reg!("SieveScript/query", backend, |b, _ci, a| sieve::handle_sieve_query(&*b, a).await);
     reg!("SieveScript/validate", backend, |b, _ci, a| sieve::handle_sieve_validate(&*b, a).await);
   }
   (Note: reg! is a private macro in lib.rs — copy its exact pattern from the mdn section)

DEFENSIVE RULES:
- Each cfg item independent — no single cfg block wrapping multiple items
- sieve.rs itself has NO cfg attributes — gates are exclusively in lib.rs
- cargo build (no features) MUST still compile cleanly after this change

AGENT TEAM: Single implementer

TESTS: cargo check -p jmap-mail-server --features sieve passes; cargo build -p jmap-mail-server (no features) passes
